KEY: LDA
ALIASES: LOAD ACCUMULATOR
SUMMARY: A <- M. IMM ZP ZPX ABS ABSX ABSY INDX INDY
BODY:
LDA - LOAD ACCUMULATOR              FLAGS: N Z
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  IMM      LDA #$12        A9  2   2
  ZP       LDA $12         A5  2   3
  ZP,X     LDA $12,X       B5  2   4
  ABS      LDA $1234       AD  3   4
  ABS,X    LDA $1234,X     BD  3  4+P
  ABS,Y    LDA $1234,Y     B9  3  4+P
  (ZP,X)   LDA ($12,X)     A1  2   6
  (ZP),Y   LDA ($12),Y     B1  2  5+P
  +P = ADD 1 CYCLE ON A PAGE CROSSING
---
KEY: LDX
ALIASES: LOAD X
SUMMARY: X <- M. IMM ZP ZPY ABS ABSY
BODY:
LDX - LOAD X                        FLAGS: N Z
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  IMM      LDX #$12        A2  2   2
  ZP       LDX $12         A6  2   3
  ZP,Y     LDX $12,Y       B6  2   4
  ABS      LDX $1234       AE  3   4
  ABS,Y    LDX $1234,Y     BE  3  4+P
  +P = ADD 1 CYCLE ON A PAGE CROSSING
---
KEY: LDY
ALIASES: LOAD Y
SUMMARY: Y <- M. IMM ZP ZPX ABS ABSX
BODY:
LDY - LOAD Y                        FLAGS: N Z
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  IMM      LDY #$12        A0  2   2
  ZP       LDY $12         A4  2   3
  ZP,X     LDY $12,X       B4  2   4
  ABS      LDY $1234       AC  3   4
  ABS,X    LDY $1234,X     BC  3  4+P
  +P = ADD 1 CYCLE ON A PAGE CROSSING
---
KEY: STA
ALIASES: STORE ACCUMULATOR
SUMMARY: M <- A. ZP ZPX ABS ABSX ABSY INDX INDY
BODY:
STA - STORE ACCUMULATOR             FLAGS: NONE
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  ZP       STA $12         85  2   3
  ZP,X     STA $12,X       95  2   4
  ABS      STA $1234       8D  3   4
  ABS,X    STA $1234,X     9D  3   5
  ABS,Y    STA $1234,Y     99  3   5
  (ZP,X)   STA ($12,X)     81  2   6
  (ZP),Y   STA ($12),Y     91  2   6

STORES HAVE FIXED TIMING: THE INDEXED FORMS ALWAYS
PERFORM A DUMMY READ BEFORE THE WRITE, SO THERE IS
NO PAGE-CROSSING DISCOUNT LIKE THE LOADS GET.
---
KEY: STX
ALIASES: STORE X
SUMMARY: M <- X. ZP ZPY ABS
BODY:
STX - STORE X                       FLAGS: NONE
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  ZP       STX $12         86  2   3
  ZP,Y     STX $12,Y       96  2   4
  ABS      STX $1234       8E  3   4
---
KEY: STY
ALIASES: STORE Y
SUMMARY: M <- Y. ZP ZPX ABS
BODY:
STY - STORE Y                       FLAGS: NONE
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  ZP       STY $12         84  2   3
  ZP,X     STY $12,X       94  2   4
  ABS      STY $1234       8C  3   4
---
KEY: TAX
SUMMARY: X <- A. Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
TAX - TRANSFER A TO X       AA  1  2  FLAGS: N Z
---
KEY: TAY
SUMMARY: Y <- A. Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
TAY - TRANSFER A TO Y       A8  1  2  FLAGS: N Z
---
KEY: TXA
SUMMARY: A <- X. Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
TXA - TRANSFER X TO A       8A  1  2  FLAGS: N Z
---
KEY: TYA
SUMMARY: A <- Y. Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
TYA - TRANSFER Y TO A       98  1  2  FLAGS: N Z
---
KEY: TSX
SUMMARY: X <- SP. Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
TSX - TRANSFER SP TO X      BA  1  2  FLAGS: N Z
---
KEY: TXS
SUMMARY: SP <- X. Implied, 2 cycles. Sets no flags
BODY:
TXS - TRANSFER X TO SP      9A  1  2  FLAGS: NONE

DELIBERATELY DOES NOT UPDATE N OR Z, UNLIKE EVERY
OTHER TRANSFER INSTRUCTION.
---
KEY: ADC
ALIASES: ADD WITH CARRY
SUMMARY: A <- A + M + C. IMM ZP ZPX ABS ABSX ABSY INDX INDY
BODY:
ADC - ADD WITH CARRY              FLAGS: N V Z C
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  IMM      ADC #$12        69  2   2
  ZP       ADC $12         65  2   3
  ZP,X     ADC $12,X       75  2   4
  ABS      ADC $1234       6D  3   4
  ABS,X    ADC $1234,X     7D  3  4+P
  ABS,Y    ADC $1234,Y     79  3  4+P
  (ZP,X)   ADC ($12,X)     61  2   6
  (ZP),Y   ADC ($12),Y     71  2  5+P
  +P = ADD 1 CYCLE ON A PAGE CROSSING

SET OR CLEAR C EXPLICITLY BEFORE A CHAIN OF ADC.
WITH D=1, PERFORMS NMOS DECIMAL (BCD) ADJUSTMENT;
SEE THE DECIMAL MODE SECTION OF THE 6502 GUIDE.
---
KEY: SBC
ALIASES: SUBTRACT WITH CARRY
SUMMARY: A <- A - M - (1-C). IMM ZP ZPX ABS ABSX ABSY INDX INDY
BODY:
SBC - SUBTRACT WITH CARRY         FLAGS: N V Z C
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  IMM      SBC #$12        E9  2   2
  ZP       SBC $12         E5  2   3
  ZP,X     SBC $12,X       F5  2   4
  ABS      SBC $1234       ED  3   4
  ABS,X    SBC $1234,X     FD  3  4+P
  ABS,Y    SBC $1234,Y     F9  3  4+P
  (ZP,X)   SBC ($12,X)     E1  2   6
  (ZP),Y   SBC ($12),Y     F1  2  5+P
  +P = ADD 1 CYCLE ON A PAGE CROSSING

$EB IS AN UNDOCUMENTED ALIAS OF THE IMMEDIATE FORM;
FANTICON'S ASSEMBLER EMITS THE OFFICIAL $E9 FOR
SBC #, SO REACH $EB WITH DFB OR HEX IF NEEDED. SET
OR CLEAR C EXPLICITLY BEFORE A CHAIN OF SBC.
---
KEY: CMP
ALIASES: COMPARE ACCUMULATOR
SUMMARY: Compute A - M, discard result. IMM ZP ZPX ABS ABSX ABSY INDX INDY
BODY:
CMP - COMPARE A                     FLAGS: N Z C
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  IMM      CMP #$12        C9  2   2
  ZP       CMP $12         C5  2   3
  ZP,X     CMP $12,X       D5  2   4
  ABS      CMP $1234       CD  3   4
  ABS,X    CMP $1234,X     DD  3  4+P
  ABS,Y    CMP $1234,Y     D9  3  4+P
  (ZP,X)   CMP ($12,X)     C1  2   6
  (ZP),Y   CMP ($12),Y     D1  2  5+P
  +P = ADD 1 CYCLE ON A PAGE CROSSING

AFTER CMP, C=1 MEANS A >= M (UNSIGNED). USE
BCC/BCS FOR LESS-THAN/GREATER-OR-EQUAL AND
BEQ/BNE FOR EQUALITY.
---
KEY: CPX
SUMMARY: Compute X - M, discard result. IMM ZP ABS
BODY:
CPX - COMPARE X                     FLAGS: N Z C
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  IMM      CPX #$12        E0  2   2
  ZP       CPX $12         E4  2   3
  ABS      CPX $1234       EC  3   4
---
KEY: CPY
SUMMARY: Compute Y - M, discard result. IMM ZP ABS
BODY:
CPY - COMPARE Y                     FLAGS: N Z C
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  IMM      CPY #$12        C0  2   2
  ZP       CPY $12         C4  2   3
  ABS      CPY $1234       CC  3   4
---
KEY: INC
SUMMARY: M <- M + 1. ZP ZPX ABS ABSX (read-modify-write)
BODY:
INC - INCREMENT MEMORY              FLAGS: N Z
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  ZP       INC $12         E6  2   5
  ZP,X     INC $12,X       F6  2   6
  ABS      INC $1234       EE  3   6
  ABS,X    INC $1234,X     FE  3   7

FIXED TIMING: READS THE OLD VALUE, WRITES IT BACK
UNCHANGED, THEN WRITES THE NEW VALUE.
---
KEY: DEC
SUMMARY: M <- M - 1. ZP ZPX ABS ABSX (read-modify-write)
BODY:
DEC - DECREMENT MEMORY              FLAGS: N Z
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  ZP       DEC $12         C6  2   5
  ZP,X     DEC $12,X       D6  2   6
  ABS      DEC $1234       CE  3   6
  ABS,X    DEC $1234,X     DE  3   7

FIXED TIMING: READS THE OLD VALUE, WRITES IT BACK
UNCHANGED, THEN WRITES THE NEW VALUE.
---
KEY: INX
SUMMARY: X <- X + 1. Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
INX - INCREMENT X           E8  1  2  FLAGS: N Z
---
KEY: INY
SUMMARY: Y <- Y + 1. Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
INY - INCREMENT Y           C8  1  2  FLAGS: N Z
---
KEY: DEX
SUMMARY: X <- X - 1. Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
DEX - DECREMENT X           CA  1  2  FLAGS: N Z
---
KEY: DEY
SUMMARY: Y <- Y - 1. Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
DEY - DECREMENT Y           88  1  2  FLAGS: N Z
---
KEY: AND
SUMMARY: A <- A & M. IMM ZP ZPX ABS ABSX ABSY INDX INDY
BODY:
AND - LOGICAL AND                   FLAGS: N Z
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  IMM      AND #$12        29  2   2
  ZP       AND $12         25  2   3
  ZP,X     AND $12,X       35  2   4
  ABS      AND $1234       2D  3   4
  ABS,X    AND $1234,X     3D  3  4+P
  ABS,Y    AND $1234,Y     39  3  4+P
  (ZP,X)   AND ($12,X)     21  2   6
  (ZP),Y   AND ($12),Y     31  2  5+P
  +P = ADD 1 CYCLE ON A PAGE CROSSING
---
KEY: ORA
SUMMARY: A <- A | M. IMM ZP ZPX ABS ABSX ABSY INDX INDY
BODY:
ORA - LOGICAL OR                    FLAGS: N Z
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  IMM      ORA #$12        09  2   2
  ZP       ORA $12         05  2   3
  ZP,X     ORA $12,X       15  2   4
  ABS      ORA $1234       0D  3   4
  ABS,X    ORA $1234,X     1D  3  4+P
  ABS,Y    ORA $1234,Y     19  3  4+P
  (ZP,X)   ORA ($12,X)     01  2   6
  (ZP),Y   ORA ($12),Y     11  2  5+P
  +P = ADD 1 CYCLE ON A PAGE CROSSING
---
KEY: EOR
ALIASES: EXCLUSIVE OR
SUMMARY: A <- A ^ M. IMM ZP ZPX ABS ABSX ABSY INDX INDY
BODY:
EOR - LOGICAL EXCLUSIVE OR          FLAGS: N Z
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  IMM      EOR #$12        49  2   2
  ZP       EOR $12         45  2   3
  ZP,X     EOR $12,X       55  2   4
  ABS      EOR $1234       4D  3   4
  ABS,X    EOR $1234,X     5D  3  4+P
  ABS,Y    EOR $1234,Y     59  3  4+P
  (ZP,X)   EOR ($12,X)     41  2   6
  (ZP),Y   EOR ($12),Y     51  2  5+P
  +P = ADD 1 CYCLE ON A PAGE CROSSING
---
KEY: BIT
SUMMARY: Test A & M; copy M bits 7/6 to N/V. ZP ABS
BODY:
BIT - BIT TEST                      FLAGS: N V Z
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  ZP       BIT $12         24  2   3
  ABS      BIT $1234       2C  3   4

DOES NOT CHANGE A. Z COMES FROM A & M; N AND V ARE
COPIED DIRECTLY FROM BITS 7 AND 6 OF M, NOT FROM
THE AND RESULT. USEFUL FOR TESTING A MASK OR
READING FLAG-LIKE BITS FROM A HARDWARE REGISTER
WITHOUT DISTURBING A.
---
KEY: ASL
SUMMARY: Shift left, bit 7 -> C. A ZP ZPX ABS ABSX
BODY:
ASL - SHIFT LEFT                    FLAGS: N Z C
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  A        ASL A           0A  1   2
  ZP       ASL $12         06  2   5
  ZP,X     ASL $12,X       16  2   6
  ABS      ASL $1234       0E  3   6
  ABS,X    ASL $1234,X     1E  3   7

BIT 7 GOES TO C, BIT 0 BECOMES 0. MULTIPLICATION
BY TWO WHEN OVERFLOW IS INTENTIONALLY IGNORED.
MEMORY FORMS ARE READ-MODIFY-WRITE: FIXED TIMING,
NO PAGE DISCOUNT.
---
KEY: LSR
SUMMARY: Shift right, bit 0 -> C. A ZP ZPX ABS ABSX
BODY:
LSR - SHIFT RIGHT                   FLAGS: N Z C
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  A        LSR A           4A  1   2
  ZP       LSR $12         46  2   5
  ZP,X     LSR $12,X       56  2   6
  ABS      LSR $1234       4E  3   6
  ABS,X    LSR $1234,X     5E  3   7

BIT 0 GOES TO C, BIT 7 BECOMES 0. UNSIGNED DIVISION
BY TWO. MEMORY FORMS ARE READ-MODIFY-WRITE: FIXED
TIMING, NO PAGE DISCOUNT.
---
KEY: ROL
SUMMARY: Shift left through carry. A ZP ZPX ABS ABSX
BODY:
ROL - ROTATE LEFT                   FLAGS: N Z C
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  A        ROL A           2A  1   2
  ZP       ROL $12         26  2   5
  ZP,X     ROL $12,X       36  2   6
  ABS      ROL $1234       2E  3   6
  ABS,X    ROL $1234,X     3E  3   7

C FEEDS INTO BIT 0 AND BIT 7 FEEDS OUT TO C. CHAIN
WITH ANOTHER ROL TO SHIFT A MULTI-BYTE VALUE LEFT.
MEMORY FORMS ARE READ-MODIFY-WRITE: FIXED TIMING.
---
KEY: ROR
SUMMARY: Shift right through carry. A ZP ZPX ABS ABSX
BODY:
ROR - ROTATE RIGHT                  FLAGS: N Z C
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  A        ROR A           6A  1   2
  ZP       ROR $12         66  2   5
  ZP,X     ROR $12,X       76  2   6
  ABS      ROR $1234       6E  3   6
  ABS,X    ROR $1234,X     7E  3   7

C FEEDS INTO BIT 7 AND BIT 0 FEEDS OUT TO C. CHAIN
WITH ANOTHER ROR TO SHIFT A MULTI-BYTE VALUE RIGHT.
MEMORY FORMS ARE READ-MODIFY-WRITE: FIXED TIMING.
---
KEY: BCC
SUMMARY: Branch if C=0. Relative, 2+taken+page cycles
BODY:
BCC LABEL          OPCODE 90, 2 BYTES
BRANCH IF C=0.  2 CYCLES NOT TAKEN, 3 TAKEN ON THE
SAME PAGE, 4 TAKEN ACROSS A PAGE BOUNDARY.
REACH IS -128..+127 FROM THE ADDRESS AFTER THE
OPERAND. FOR A LONGER JUMP, INVERT THE CONDITION
AND JMP:  BCS NEARBY / JMP FAR / NEARBY:
---
KEY: BCS
SUMMARY: Branch if C=1. Relative, 2+taken+page cycles
BODY:
BCS LABEL          OPCODE B0, 2 BYTES
BRANCH IF C=1. SEE THE BCC CARD FOR TIMING AND THE
LONG-BRANCH IDIOM (INVERT AND JMP).
---
KEY: BEQ
SUMMARY: Branch if Z=1. Relative, 2+taken+page cycles
BODY:
BEQ LABEL          OPCODE F0, 2 BYTES
BRANCH IF Z=1 (EQUAL, AFTER CMP/CPX/CPY OR ANY
FLAG-SETTING OP). SEE THE BCC CARD FOR TIMING AND
THE LONG-BRANCH IDIOM.
---
KEY: BNE
SUMMARY: Branch if Z=0. Relative, 2+taken+page cycles
BODY:
BNE LABEL          OPCODE D0, 2 BYTES
BRANCH IF Z=0 (NOT EQUAL). THE CLASSIC "DEX / BNE
LOOP" COUNTED-LOOP IDIOM. SEE THE BCC CARD FOR
TIMING AND THE LONG-BRANCH IDIOM.
---
KEY: BMI
SUMMARY: Branch if N=1. Relative, 2+taken+page cycles
BODY:
BMI LABEL          OPCODE 30, 2 BYTES
BRANCH IF N=1 (RESULT'S BIT 7 SET). SEE THE BCC
CARD FOR TIMING AND THE LONG-BRANCH IDIOM.
---
KEY: BPL
SUMMARY: Branch if N=0. Relative, 2+taken+page cycles
BODY:
BPL LABEL          OPCODE 10, 2 BYTES
BRANCH IF N=0. SEE THE BCC CARD FOR TIMING AND THE
LONG-BRANCH IDIOM.
---
KEY: BVC
SUMMARY: Branch if V=0. Relative, 2+taken+page cycles
BODY:
BVC LABEL          OPCODE 50, 2 BYTES
BRANCH IF V=0 (NO SIGNED OVERFLOW). SEE THE BCC
CARD FOR TIMING AND THE LONG-BRANCH IDIOM.
---
KEY: BVS
SUMMARY: Branch if V=1. Relative, 2+taken+page cycles
BODY:
BVS LABEL          OPCODE 70, 2 BYTES
BRANCH IF V=1 (SIGNED OVERFLOW). SEE THE BCC CARD
FOR TIMING AND THE LONG-BRANCH IDIOM.
---
KEY: JMP
SUMMARY: PC <- address. Absolute or (indirect)
BODY:
JMP - JUMP                          FLAGS: NONE
  MODE       SYNTAX        OP  B  CYC
  ABS        JMP $1234     4C  3   3
  INDIRECT   JMP ($1234)   6C  3   5

THE ORIGINAL NMOS PAGE-WRAP BUG APPLIES TO THE
INDIRECT FORM: IF THE POINTER IS AT $12FF, THE HIGH
BYTE OF THE DESTINATION IS READ FROM $1200, NOT
$1300. FANTICON MATCHES THIS EXACTLY; AVOID PLACING
AN INDIRECT-JUMP POINTER ACROSS A PAGE BOUNDARY.
---
KEY: JSR
SUMMARY: Push return address, then jump. Absolute, 6 cycles
BODY:
JSR $1234          OPCODE 20, 3 BYTES, 6 CYCLES
PUSHES THE ADDRESS OF THE LAST BYTE OF THE JSR
INSTRUCTION ITSELF (NOT THE NEXT INSTRUCTION), THEN
JUMPS. RTS PULLS THAT VALUE AND ADDS ONE. PAIR JSR
WITH RTS; DO NOT RETURN FROM A SUBROUTINE WITH RTI.
---
KEY: RTS
SUMMARY: Pull return address, add one, return. Implied
BODY:
RTS                OPCODE 60, 1 BYTE, 6 CYCLES
RETURNS FROM A JSR. SEE THE JSR CARD FOR WHY THE
PULLED ADDRESS IS INCREMENTED.
---
KEY: RTI
SUMMARY: Pull status and PC. Implied, 6 cycles
BODY:
RTI                OPCODE 40, 1 BYTE, 6 CYCLES
RETURNS FROM AN INTERRUPT HANDLER (IRQ, NMI, OR
BRK), RESTORING BOTH STATUS AND PC. USE RTI ONLY TO
RETURN FROM AN INTERRUPT, NEVER TO RETURN FROM A
JSR.
---
KEY: PHA
SUMMARY: Push A. Implied, 3 cycles
BODY:
PHA                OPCODE 48, 1 BYTE, 3 CYCLES
FLAGS: NONE. PUSHES A ONTO THE STACK AT $0100+SP,
THEN DECREMENTS SP.
---
KEY: PHP
SUMMARY: Push status (B=1). Implied, 3 cycles
BODY:
PHP                OPCODE 08, 1 BYTE, 3 CYCLES
FLAGS: NONE. PUSHES STATUS WITH THE B BIT AND THE
UNUSED BIT BOTH SET TO 1. B IS A MARKER IN THE
PUSHED BYTE, NOT A PERSISTENT CPU FLAG.
---
KEY: PLA
SUMMARY: Pull A. Implied, 4 cycles
BODY:
PLA                OPCODE 68, 1 BYTE, 4 CYCLES
FLAGS: N Z. INCREMENTS SP, THEN READS A FROM
$0100+SP.
---
KEY: PLP
SUMMARY: Pull status. Implied, 4 cycles
BODY:
PLP                OPCODE 28, 1 BYTE, 4 CYCLES
FLAGS: FULLY RESTORED FROM THE STACK.
---
KEY: BRK
SUMMARY: Software interrupt through $FFFE/$FFFF
BODY:
BRK                OPCODE 00, 7 CYCLES. FLAGS: I SET

BRK IS A TWO-BYTE OPERATION IN PRACTICE: THE CPU
INCREMENTS PC PAST THE BYTE FOLLOWING THE OPCODE
BEFORE STACKING IT, SO DEBUGGERS AND INLINE-DATA
SCHEMES MUST ACCOUNT FOR THAT PADDING/SIGNATURE
BYTE. PUSHES PC AND STATUS (WITH B=1), SETS I, THEN
LOADS PC FROM $FFFE/$FFFF. RETURN WITH RTI.
---
KEY: CLC
SUMMARY: C <- 0. Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
CLC                OPCODE 18, 1 BYTE, 2 CYCLES
CLEARS THE CARRY FLAG. DO THIS BEFORE AN ADC CHAIN.
---
KEY: SEC
SUMMARY: C <- 1. Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
SEC                OPCODE 38, 1 BYTE, 2 CYCLES
SETS THE CARRY FLAG. DO THIS BEFORE AN SBC CHAIN.
---
KEY: CLI
SUMMARY: I <- 0 (enable IRQ). Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
CLI                OPCODE 58, 1 BYTE, 2 CYCLES
ENABLES MASKABLE IRQ RECOGNITION. NMOS
INTERRUPT-POLLING IS CYCLE-SPECIFIC AROUND CLI; AN
ALREADY-ASSERTED IRQ IS NORMALLY RECOGNIZED AFTER
ONE MORE INSTRUCTION.
---
KEY: SEI
SUMMARY: I <- 1 (disable IRQ). Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
SEI                OPCODE 78, 1 BYTE, 2 CYCLES
DISABLES MASKABLE IRQ RECOGNITION. AN IRQ ASSERTED
RIGHT AROUND SEI CAN STILL BE TAKEN BASED ON THE
OLD I VALUE; AVOID DEPENDING ON THAT EDGE CASE
OUTSIDE TIMING-SENSITIVE LOW-LEVEL CODE.
---
KEY: CLD
SUMMARY: D <- 0 (binary arithmetic). Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
CLD                OPCODE D8, 1 BYTE, 2 CYCLES
NMOS RESET AND INTERRUPT ENTRY DO NOT CLEAR D. SET
IT EXPLICITLY AT RESET AND AT THE START OF AN
INTERRUPT HANDLER THAT USES ARITHMETIC.
---
KEY: SED
SUMMARY: D <- 1 (decimal/BCD arithmetic). Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
SED                OPCODE F8, 1 BYTE, 2 CYCLES
ENABLES BCD ADJUSTMENT IN ADC/SBC. PREFER KEEPING
DECIMAL MODE CLEAR EXCEPT INSIDE A SMALL, DELIBERATE
BCD ROUTINE; RETURN TO CLD AFTERWARD.
---
KEY: CLV
SUMMARY: V <- 0. Implied, 2 cycles
BODY:
CLV                OPCODE B8, 1 BYTE, 2 CYCLES
CLEARS THE OVERFLOW FLAG. THERE IS NO SEV.
---
KEY: NOP
SUMMARY: No result. Implied, 2 cycles (see undocumented forms)
BODY:
NOP                OPCODE EA, 1 BYTE, 2 CYCLES
FLAGS: NONE. NO REGISTER OR MEMORY RESULT.

FANTICON'S ASSEMBLER ALSO ACCEPTS ADDRESSED NOP
FORMS FOR SIZE/TIMING PADDING, EMITTING A STABLE
CANONICAL BYTE PER MODE: $80 (IMM), $04 (ZP), $14
(ZP,X), $0C (ABS), $1C (ABS,X). THESE STILL PERFORM
THE NORMAL ADDRESSING-MODE BUS READS, SO THEY ARE
NOT ALL EQUIVALENT TO EA.
---
KEY: KIL
ALIASES: JAM, HALT
SUMMARY: Undocumented: halt until RESET
BODY:
KIL
JAM                (SAME OPCODE; JAM IS AN ALIAS)

CANONICAL BYTE $02. OTHER JAM/KIL ENCODINGS EXIST
AT $12 $22 $32 $42 $52 $62 $72 $92 $B2 $D2 $F2; USE
DFB/HEX FOR A SPECIFIC ALTERNATE BYTE.

EXECUTING ONE HALTS USEFUL INSTRUCTION EXECUTION
UNTIL RESET. NOT A NORMAL WAIT PRIMITIVE — ONLY USE
IT WHEN DELIBERATELY HANDING CONTROL BACK TO A
RESET MECHANISM (E.G. AS A CRASH TRAP).
---
KEY: SLO
SUMMARY: Undocumented: ASL M, then A <- A | M
BODY:
SLO - SHIFT LEFT THEN OR      (UNDOCUMENTED)
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  (ZP,X)   SLO ($12,X)     03  2   8
  ZP       SLO $12         07  2   5
  ABS      SLO $1234       0F  3   6
  (ZP),Y   SLO ($12),Y     13  2   8
  ZP,X     SLO $12,X       17  2   6
  ABS,Y    SLO $1234,Y     1B  3   7
  ABS,X    SLO $1234,X     1F  3   7

READ-MODIFY-WRITE: PERFORMS THE ASL, THEN ORs THE
SHIFTED VALUE INTO A. FIXED TIMING, NO PAGE
DISCOUNT.
---
KEY: RLA
SUMMARY: Undocumented: ROL M, then A <- A & M
BODY:
RLA - ROTATE LEFT THEN AND    (UNDOCUMENTED)
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  (ZP,X)   RLA ($12,X)     23  2   8
  ZP       RLA $12         27  2   5
  ABS      RLA $1234       2F  3   6
  (ZP),Y   RLA ($12),Y     33  2   8
  ZP,X     RLA $12,X       37  2   6
  ABS,Y    RLA $1234,Y     3B  3   7
  ABS,X    RLA $1234,X     3F  3   7

READ-MODIFY-WRITE: PERFORMS THE ROL, THEN ANDs THE
ROTATED VALUE INTO A. FIXED TIMING, NO PAGE
DISCOUNT.
---
KEY: SRE
SUMMARY: Undocumented: LSR M, then A <- A ^ M
BODY:
SRE - SHIFT RIGHT THEN EOR    (UNDOCUMENTED)
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  (ZP,X)   SRE ($12,X)     43  2   8
  ZP       SRE $12         47  2   5
  ABS      SRE $1234       4F  3   6
  (ZP),Y   SRE ($12),Y     53  2   8
  ZP,X     SRE $12,X       57  2   6
  ABS,Y    SRE $1234,Y     5B  3   7
  ABS,X    SRE $1234,X     5F  3   7

READ-MODIFY-WRITE: PERFORMS THE LSR, THEN EORs THE
SHIFTED VALUE INTO A. FIXED TIMING, NO PAGE
DISCOUNT.
---
KEY: RRA
SUMMARY: Undocumented: ROR M, then ADC M
BODY:
RRA - ROTATE RIGHT THEN ADC   (UNDOCUMENTED)
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  (ZP,X)   RRA ($12,X)     63  2   8
  ZP       RRA $12         67  2   5
  ABS      RRA $1234       6F  3   6
  (ZP),Y   RRA ($12),Y     73  2   8
  ZP,X     RRA $12,X       77  2   6
  ABS,Y    RRA $1234,Y     7B  3   7
  ABS,X    RRA $1234,X     7F  3   7

READ-MODIFY-WRITE: PERFORMS THE ROR, THEN ADCs THE
ROTATED VALUE INTO A. FIXED TIMING, NO PAGE
DISCOUNT.
---
KEY: SAX
SUMMARY: Undocumented store: M <- A & X
BODY:
SAX - STORE A AND X           (UNDOCUMENTED)
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  (ZP,X)   SAX ($12,X)     83  2   6
  ZP       SAX $12         87  2   3
  ABS      SAX $1234       8F  3   4
  ZP,Y     SAX $12,Y       97  2   4

STORES A & X WITHOUT CHANGING EITHER REGISTER.
DETERMINISTIC AND STABLE, UNLIKE THE AHX/TAS/SHX/
SHY FAMILY.
---
KEY: LAX
SUMMARY: Undocumented: A <- M; X <- M
BODY:
LAX - LOAD A AND X            (UNDOCUMENTED)
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  (ZP,X)   LAX ($12,X)     A3  2   6
  ZP       LAX $12         A7  2   3
  ABS      LAX $1234       AF  3   4
  (ZP),Y   LAX ($12),Y     B3  2  5+P
  ZP,Y     LAX $12,Y       B7  2   4
  ABS,Y    LAX $1234,Y     BF  3  4+P
  IMM      LAX #$12        AB  2   2  (UNSTABLE)
  +P = ADD 1 CYCLE ON A PAGE CROSSING

THE SIX MEMORY MODES ARE DETERMINISTIC: A AND X
BOTH GET M. THE IMMEDIATE FORM ($AB) IS THE
UNSTABLE ONE: A <- X <- (A | $EE) & #. FANTICON
REPRODUCES THE DETERMINISTIC $EE-MASK BEHAVIOR OF
ITS NMOS CONFORMANCE MODEL FOR IT.
---
KEY: DCP
SUMMARY: Undocumented: DEC M, then compare A with M
BODY:
DCP - DECREMENT THEN COMPARE  (UNDOCUMENTED)
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  (ZP,X)   DCP ($12,X)     C3  2   8
  ZP       DCP $12         C7  2   5
  ABS      DCP $1234       CF  3   6
  (ZP),Y   DCP ($12),Y     D3  2   8
  ZP,X     DCP $12,X       D7  2   6
  ABS,Y    DCP $1234,Y     DB  3   7
  ABS,X    DCP $1234,X     DF  3   7

READ-MODIFY-WRITE: DECREMENTS M, THEN COMPARES A
WITH THE DECREMENTED VALUE (SAME FLAG EFFECT AS
CMP). FIXED TIMING, NO PAGE DISCOUNT.
---
KEY: ISC
ALIASES: ISB
SUMMARY: Undocumented: INC M, then SBC M
BODY:
ISC - INCREMENT THEN SBC      (UNDOCUMENTED)
ISB                (SAME OPCODE; ISB IS AN ALIAS)
  MODE     SYNTAX          OP  B  CYC
  (ZP,X)   ISC ($12,X)     E3  2   8
  ZP       ISC $12         E7  2   5
  ABS      ISC $1234       EF  3   6
  (ZP),Y   ISC ($12),Y     F3  2   8
  ZP,X     ISC $12,X       F7  2   6
  ABS,Y    ISC $1234,Y     FB  3   7
  ABS,X    ISC $1234,X     FF  3   7

READ-MODIFY-WRITE: INCREMENTS M, THEN SUBTRACTS THE
INCREMENTED VALUE FROM A WITH BORROW (SAME FLAG
EFFECT AS SBC). FIXED TIMING, NO PAGE DISCOUNT.
---
KEY: ANC
SUMMARY: Undocumented: A <- A & #; C <- result bit 7
BODY:
ANC #imm         OPCODE 0B (CANONICAL; 2B DUPLICATE)
2 BYTES, 2 CYCLES.  FLAGS: N Z C

ANDS A WITH THE IMMEDIATE OPERAND, THEN COPIES BIT
7 OF THE RESULT INTO C — USEFUL FOR A COMBINED
MASK-AND-CARRY-TEST IN ONE INSTRUCTION.
---
KEY: ALR
SUMMARY: Undocumented: A <- A & #, then LSR A
BODY:
ALR #imm          OPCODE 4B, 2 BYTES, 2 CYCLES

ANDS A WITH THE IMMEDIATE OPERAND, THEN LOGICALLY
SHIFTS THE RESULT RIGHT ONE BIT (SAME FLAG EFFECT
AS LSR).
---
KEY: ARR
SUMMARY: Undocumented: A <- A & #, then ROR A
BODY:
ARR #imm          OPCODE 6B, 2 BYTES, 2 CYCLES

ANDS A WITH THE IMMEDIATE OPERAND, THEN ROTATES THE
RESULT RIGHT THROUGH CARRY. HAS UNUSUAL C/V AND
DECIMAL-MODE BEHAVIOR THAT DIFFERS FROM A PLAIN
AND+ROR SEQUENCE; VERIFY AGAINST FANTICON'S TESTS
BEFORE RELYING ON THE FLAG RESULT IN DECIMAL MODE.
---
KEY: XAA
SUMMARY: Undocumented, unstable: A <- (A|$EE) & X & #
BODY:
XAA #imm           OPCODE 8B, 2 BYTES, 2 CYCLES
FLAGS: N Z

UNSTABLE ON REAL SILICON; FANTICON REPRODUCES A
DETERMINISTIC $EE-MASK BEHAVIOR. AVOID UNLESS
FANTICON ITSELF IS THE ONLY TARGET.
---
KEY: AXS
ALIASES: SBX
SUMMARY: Undocumented: X <- (A & X) - #
BODY:
AXS #imm
SBX #imm           (SAME OPCODE; SBX IS AN ALIAS)
OPCODE CB, 2 BYTES, 2 CYCLES

X BECOMES (A & X) MINUS THE IMMEDIATE OPERAND, AS
AN UNSIGNED SUBTRACTION. C REPORTS NO-BORROW, THE
SAME CONVENTION CMP/SBC USE.
---
KEY: AHX
SUMMARY: Undocumented, unstable: high-byte-masked store
BODY:
AHX (zp),Y         OPCODE 93, 2 BYTES, 6 CYCLES
AHX abs,Y          OPCODE 9F, 3 BYTES, 5 CYCLES

LET H BE THE UNINDEXED BASE ADDRESS'S HIGH BYTE
PLUS ONE (WRAPPING AT 8 BITS). WRITES A & X & H. IF
INDEXING CROSSES A PAGE, THE WRITTEN VALUE ALSO
REPLACES THE DESTINATION ADDRESS'S HIGH BYTE. THIS
ADDRESS CORRUPTION IS PART OF THE EMULATED NMOS
BEHAVIOR, NOT A BUG. FANTICON TARGET ONLY.
---
KEY: TAS
SUMMARY: Undocumented, unstable: SP <- A & X, then masked store
BODY:
TAS abs,Y          OPCODE 9B, 3 BYTES, 5 CYCLES

SETS SP TO A & X, THEN WRITES SP & H (SEE THE AHX
CARD FOR H). SAME ADDRESS-CORRUPTION-ON-PAGE-CROSS
BEHAVIOR AS AHX. FANTICON TARGET ONLY.
---
KEY: SHY
SUMMARY: Undocumented, unstable: store Y masked by high byte
BODY:
SHY abs,X          OPCODE 9C, 3 BYTES, 5 CYCLES

WRITES Y & H (SEE THE AHX CARD FOR H). SAME
ADDRESS-CORRUPTION-ON-PAGE-CROSS BEHAVIOR AS AHX.
FANTICON TARGET ONLY.
---
KEY: SHX
SUMMARY: Undocumented, unstable: store X masked by high byte
BODY:
SHX abs,Y          OPCODE 9E, 3 BYTES, 5 CYCLES

WRITES X & H (SEE THE AHX CARD FOR H). SAME
ADDRESS-CORRUPTION-ON-PAGE-CROSS BEHAVIOR AS AHX.
FANTICON TARGET ONLY.
---
KEY: LAS
SUMMARY: Undocumented: A <- X <- SP <- M & SP
BODY:
LAS abs,Y          OPCODE BB, 3 BYTES, 4+P CYCLES
+P = ADD 1 CYCLE ON A PAGE CROSSING

ANDS THE MEMORY OPERAND WITH SP AND WRITES THE
RESULT TO A, X, AND SP ALL AT ONCE.
---
